# Build the screen the usual way

Build the feature the way other products already do it. Read the design and the requirements before inventing a control or a loading state.

A decision about one screen's fields stays in that screen's docs. It does not become a rule for every screen.

## Do

- Search updates the results only. The title, the search box, the buttons, and the section headings stay on screen.
- Navigation (the tab bar, back buttons) stays visible while data loads.

## Do not

- Replace a screen with a skeleton because a query is in flight. Skeleton only the values still loading. See `skeletons-match-the-screen.mdc`.
- Copy one screen's field decisions into an always-on rule.
